<title>CANADA: DBRS confirms British Columbia ratings AT AA, R-1.</title>
<headline>DBRS confirms British Columbia ratings AT AA, R-1.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dominion Bond Rating Service said it confirmed the credit ratings for the Province of British Columbia at AA for long-term obligations and R-1 (middle) for short-term obligations.</p>
<p>The Toronto-based ratings agency said all ratings were given a stable trend.</p>
<p>DBRS said the ratings reflect the province's low debt level relative to gross domestic product, a relatively well diversified economy with a large natural resource base and a &quot;realistic&quot; medium term financial management plan.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
</text>
